A||||7||MooCow||My car squeeks when getting out!||||9||
Z||000000||MooCow||06-18-2001||11:11 PM||||Well now everytime I get out of the car it make a squeek noise.  It only happens when you get out of the drivers side.  It sounds like it is comming from the back tire area.  so I sprayed the shocks and what and not and it still squeeks.  Its not like a little squeek but sorta long and quiet, but you can still hear it.  Anyone have any ideas on how to make it stop??  I know if I get out really, really slow it won't do it.<P>                                 Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-18-2001||11:21 PM||||It still might be the shocks settling, something inside them might be squeeking, and spraying them with something won't fix that. <P>Have someone stand outside the car when you get out so you can make sure that it is something in the rear.  If the shocks are newer, I don't think that they should be making much noise at all.<P>The only other suggestion I could offer is maybe the cradle bushings are squeeking in thier housings as you get out of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||06-18-2001||11:52 PM||||Do you have any urethane bushings?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||06-19-2001||08:39 AM||||It's either you back or your knees depending on how old you are.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||06-19-2001||10:31 AM||||Make sure the metal backing plate, behind the brake rotor, is not touching the control arm. This happened on my S-10. Made me crazy for months.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
